From: uDroid graphics runtime
Subject: [PATCH] libhybris: support relocatable runtime linking

Libtool normally records the configured installation directory as RUNPATH in
libraries that depend on another libhybris library. That makes a staged
runtime depend on the build-time prefix and can also preserve a build-root
path when uninstalled .libs artifacts are packaged accidentally.

Add an opt-in configure switch that keeps -L available for install-time
relinking without emitting an absolute runtime search path. uDroid launches
the colocated libraries with an explicit component-local LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
---
 hybris/configure.ac | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hybris/configure.ac b/hybris/configure.ac
index 54e5042..1f2339f 100644
--- a/hybris/configure.ac
+++ b/hybris/configure.ac
@@ -20,7 +20,17 @@ AC_GNU_SOURCE
 AC_DISABLE_STATIC
 AC_PROG_LIBTOOL
 AM_PROG_AS
+
+AC_ARG_ENABLE([relocatable-runtime],
+  [AS_HELP_STRING([--enable-relocatable-runtime],
+    [do not encode the configured libdir as an ELF runtime search path])],
+  [relocatable_runtime=$enableval],
+  [relocatable_runtime=no])
+AS_IF([test x"$relocatable_runtime" = x"yes"], [
+  hardcode_libdir_flag_spec='-L$libdir'
+  hardcode_libdir_flag_spec_CXX='-L$libdir'
+])
 
 AC_SUBST(CFLAGS)
 AC_SUBST(CPPFLAGS)
 AC_SUBST(LDFLAGS)
-- 
2.50.1
